# Part 2: Fitting a Poisson Model

## Mini-tutorial: Fitting and reading a Poisson model

Before you fit your model on the GSS data, here is a worked example on a toy dataset so you can see the full workflow.

**Toy data:**


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
toy <- tibble(
  visits = c(0, 1, 3, 2, 0, 5, 1, 4, 7, 2),
  age = c(22, 25, 35, 30, 20, 55, 28, 45, 60, 33)
)
```
:::


**Fit the model:**


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
toy_model <- glm(visits ~ age, data = toy, family = poisson(link = "log"))
```
:::


**Read the output on the log scale.** These coefficients are on the log-count scale. The intercept is the log of the expected count when age = 0. The slope is the change in log-count for a one-year increase in age.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
model_parameters(toy_model) %>% print_html()
```

