### Exercise 2.2 {.unnumbered}

Pick one observation from your data. Using the coefficients from your fitted model, manually compute the predicted count for that observation. Show your work, then confirm it matches the output of `predict(model, type = "response")` for that row.

::: {.callout-tip collapse="true" title="Hint: From log-counts to counts"}
The model estimates log(λ). So the predicted log-count for observation *i* is β₀ + β₁x₁ + β₂x₂ + ... Exponentiate to get the predicted count: λ = exp(β₀ + β₁x₁ + ...). Use `coef(model)` to extract the coefficients.
:::


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
