# Part 5: Model Comparison

### Exercise 5.1 {.unnumbered}

Compare your Poisson and negative binomial models using a likelihood ratio test and a comparison table. Interpret the test result and the AIC/BIC values. What do they tell you about relative model fit?

::: {.callout-tip collapse="true" title="Hint: Two ways to compare"}
`performance::test_likelihoodratio()` gives you a formal test. For a publication-style table, use `modelsummary(list("Poisson" = m1, "Neg. Binomial" = m2), exponentiate = TRUE, stars = TRUE)`. AIC/BIC are reported automatically.
:::


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
performance::test_likelihoodratio(wwwhr_clean, wwwhr_nb)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
