The output has two sections. "Count model coefficients" are interpreted like a regular negative binomial (log-counts, exponentiate for IRRs). "Zero-inflation model coefficients" are interpreted like logistic regression (log odds of being a structural zero). In this example, uninsured people may be more likely to avoid doctors entirely, which is a different process from how often insured people visit.

